    {
      "id": "719fd476-529d-4baa-901c-58aa1b51c1bb",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        720,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 844,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "## 🚚 AI Logistics Agent – Automated Delayed Shipment Rerouting\n\n### How it works\nOn a configurable schedule, the workflow reads all active shipments from Google Sheets and runs a code node to detect delays based on expected vs actual delivery dates. If any shipments are delayed, a Telegram summary alert fires and each delayed shipment is processed individually. For each one, alternate routes are fetched from your routing API and passed to GPT-4o-mini, which recommends the best reroute option with reasoning. Low-confidence or high-impact decisions are flagged for human approval via Slack — the workflow waits for an approve/reject response. Approved reroutes call your carrier TMS API, update the shipment record in Sheets, notify the customer by email, and log the action to the ops Slack channel. Rejected reroutes are escalated and marked for manual review.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** to the three Sheets nodes — replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID` and confirm the `Active Shipments` tab exists.\n2. Connect **OpenAI API** to the Analyze Reroute Options node.\n3. Connect **Telegram Bot API** to the Send Delay Summary node.\n4. Connect **Slack OAuth2** to the approval request, ops notification, and reroute log nodes — replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.\n5. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** and update the customer email node.\n6. Replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_ROUTING_API` and `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CARRIER_TMS_API` with your actual API endpoints and add any required auth headers.\n7. Activate the schedule trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "04bad4f6-cc24-4c67-8f16-072f63a7d3d5",
      "name": "Section – Scheduled Delay Detection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1632,
        -752
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1540,
        "height": 488,
        "content": "## ⏰ Scheduled Delay Detection\nRuns on a schedule. Reads all active shipments from Google Sheets, calculates which are overdue based on expected delivery dates, builds a delay summary, and fires a Telegram alert. If no delays are found, the flow exits early."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "48cb1f15-e98f-4122-8504-01fccf557ed6",
      "name": "Section – AI Alternate Route Analysis",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2848,
        -224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1296,
        "height": 456,
        "content": "## 🤖 AI Alternate Route Analysis\nEach delayed shipment is split and processed individually. Alternate routes are fetched from a routing API, then GPT-4o-mini analyses the options and returns a recommendation — best route, reasoning, and a confidence score. The output is parsed into a structured object."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c793d2cb-3b75-4109-bc3f-9142e4e57dd1",
      "name": "Section – Human Approval Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4208,
        -544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1140,
        "height": 776,
        "content": "## ✅ Human Approval Gate\nHigh-impact or low-confidence reroutes are held for human review via a Slack approval message. The workflow waits for an approve or reject response. Rejected reroutes are escalated and marked for manual review in Sheets. Approved reroutes (and auto-approved low-risk ones) proceed to carrier update."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "037f2da3-7b72-4a51-b0e1-1e8f8c9b3ca8",
      "name": "Section – Reroute Execution & Customer Notification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5376,
        -544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1272,
        "height": 616,
        "content": "## 📦 Reroute Execution & Customer Notification\nApproved reroutes call the carrier TMS API to update the route, write the new routing record to Sheets, email the customer with the updated delivery details, and post a confirmation to the ops Slack channel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
